From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:50:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/33] pipewire: let the consumer pick a tiled modifier for
 packed RGB

The capture node offers its dmabufs as DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR and nothing
else, as a one-value choice. A consumer whose importer prefers the
device's tiled layouts has to take a pitch-linear image, and one that
lists a tiled modifier first fails the link outright: without
DONT_FIXATE the filter fixates the consumer's default against our single
value.

List what the device can really do. vulkan_get_capture_modifiers keeps
the modifiers of the format that have one memory plane, support storage
images and can be exported as a dmabuf, which is the usage a capture
texture is created with. They go out ahead of LINEAR with
SPA_POD_PROP_FLAG_DONT_FIXATE. When the negotiated format still carries
that flag, param_changed settles on the first of ours the consumer kept
and republishes that one pod ahead of the full list, which is the
two-step handshake Mutter and KWin already use. A consumer that lists
LINEAR alone still gets LINEAR, and every third round in a row settles
on LINEAR so a consumer that never converges still gets a stream.

CVulkanTexture::createFlags gains ulDrmModifier: allocate with exactly
that modifier, in device memory, and export it. The planar formats stay
LINEAR because the dmabuf path exports a single plane.
